      "writtenOn": "2022-07-07T14:46:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This design allows `initialiseAxes` to be called multiple times so this class has a bunch of mutable state. In the event this returns `false` the old state is kept instead of cleared. Is that intentional? If not, it seems like this could all go into the body of the constructor? Just returning early from the constructor would leave the `fSliderAxes` at zero size, which is plenty of signal without setting a separate `bool`?",
