        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-07T14:46:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I know this is just tool code, but it\u0027s actually hard to follow the creation of a temporary `SkString` (for each axis for each frame) when we know that we\u0027re just going to pass a pointer to 5 bytes. Probably better to store the `SkString` on the `SliderAxis` (it is the name of the slider) so the construction is only done once (and can be something else, like include the name if wanted).\n\nStoring the SkString would also make it easier to add a \"prefix\" which could be passed to the constructor (say, the font name, or typeface id, or some such) so that it would be possible to have sliders for multiple axes.\n\nNote that it is allowed to add multiple controls with the same name. It works but then when one goes to read values only one of them can be read by id (need to iterate to get the others). So this setup only kinda works when a font has multiple axes with the same tag. In the future we may want some special handling for that.",
      "revId": "0a8c99d76682ceff06213671fc780f2138886ab2",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
